# name: English
#
# spacemap language file. Lines are KEY=value; blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Where a value needs to include a runtime
# value (a count, a path, a size...) the template contains a literal %s —
# one per value, filled in left-to-right order. You can move a %s to a
# different place in the sentence, but don't remove or duplicate it, and
# don't translate it into something else.
#
# The languages in lang/ are built into spacemap. To add a language,
# copy this file to lang/<language-code>.lang (e.g. nl.lang), translate the
# right-hand side of each line, set the first line to
# "# name: <language name as it should read in the settings list>", and
# add it to the list in src/lang.rs. Without rebuilding, the same file in
# ~/.config/spacemap/lang/ also works, and a file there with the code of a
# built-in language overrides just the lines it contains. Any key missing
# from a language shows in English.

